title: a humble way to share the schema
pid: 7ae1c489-6a1e-4eb4-9ce4-effb50be0e76
body: |2-
  I feel stongly about this data structure,
  the definition of atoms and the set of relationships on atoms.
  Each person owes it to themselves to keep a collection of atoms,
  to read and edit what they have collected,
  to share some of them with society,
  to read some of what society shares with them,
  and to integrate some of others' knowledge into their own.

  I don't feel strongly about how to view and edit this data structure.
  I built a program, [[skg]], that allows me to.
  It is not beautiful or friendly, but it does the job.
  You could probably write your own with AI pretty easily.
